## Highlights
Earth-abundant, cheap, and non-toxic $\mathrm{Fe(III)}$ species were anchored to the $\mathbf{Zr}_{6}$ nodes of the mesoporous MOF, PCN-222(Fe), via a post-synthetic cluster metalation strategy denoted herein as Fe@PCN-222(Fe) Fe@PCN-222(Fe) showed a remarkable activity for light-induced one-pot tandem reaction of 2- aminobenzaimde and alcohols to quinazoline- $4(3H)$ -ones The bioinspired MOF showed a higher catalytic activity than the of the bare PCN-222(Fe) and the corresponding homogeneous catalysts   
The porous heterobimetallic MOF acts as both a photoredox and Lewis acid catalyst   
Fe@PCN-222(Fe) can be reused without loss of stability or structure.
